  *** Installation ***

   1. Stop the BBS.  Unzip the release into the BBS directory:
      DIALDOS.DLL, DIALDOS.MDF, DIALDOS.MSG and DIALDOS.RLN go in the
      BBS directory, and DIALDOS.VIR goes in its GCVIRDAT folder.
   2. Start the BBS.  The first time it starts, DS-DOS creates DIALDOS.DAT
      from GCVIRDAT\DIALDOS.VIR (or from DIALDOS.VIR in the BBS
      directory).  An existing DIALDOS.DAT is never overwritten.
   3. Add "DS-DOS Shell" to your menu tree.
   4. CNF Options: None!  All settings are changed online with the
      "config" command (master key holders only).
   5. New installs start with: sysop key SYSOP, master password SYSOP
      (master password not enabled), uploads/downloads recorded in the
      audit trail, and batch file protection on.  Use "config" to change
      them.

   The DIALDOS.DAT record layout is unchanged from the WorldGroup
   releases.

  ==========================================================================

  *** Features & Usage ***

   . Supports most of the standard commands that Microsoft MS-Dos 6.22
     offers you.
   . Typing "HELP" or "?" in the shell will give you help.  For help
     on commands, type "HELP <command>" or "<command> /?"
   . MS-DOS Style Commands supported:
      dir          del/erase      pause
      ver          ren/rename     echo
      chkdsk       type/more      vol
      cd/chdir     edit           label
      md/mkdir     copy           prompt
      rd/rmdir     xcopy          time
      cls          move           date
      set          attrib
   . DialSoft DS-DOS commands:
      history
      clear
      user
      users
      grep
      colors
   . Switches supported (various commands): /S /P /Y |MORE /B /W /L
   . You can run BATCH files within DS-DOS if they include commands
     that are understood by DS-DOS!  Try it out!
     Simply use the batch file as you would normally, and it'll run!
     Commands that are not recognized by DS-Dos are ignored.
   . Use CTRL-C to abort commands/listings as you would normally
     do in MS-DOS!
   . Almost every possible form of DIR is supported!  Switches I have
     currently implemented are:
       /P - Pausing every page
       /S - Subdirectory listings!
       /Ax - Attribute listings (Archive,Directory,System,Readonly,Hidden)
       /W - Wide mode
       /B - Brief mode (only filenames listed)
       /L - Lowercase output
     I'll work on sorting /Oxx parameters next!
   . You may use the "| more" operation to pause screen ouput, similar
     to the way it works in MS-DOS. You can not redirect to anything
     other than "more".  I personally have not used the "|" operator
     on anything but "more" but if someone has a suggestion, let me
     know!
      Examples:  dir /s |more
                 type test.txt |more
   . The XCOPY command *WILL* work with the /S parameter to copy all
     subdirectories.  It will copy ALL subdirectories in a directory
     whether they have files or not.  (/E parameter is ignored, but
     it will copy empty subdirectories)
   . Cursor UP and DOWN at the command prompt!  Works just like DOSKEY
     does in MS-DOS.  You can backspace through the commands to edit
     them as well, I like to call it DIALKEY!
   . The > redirector will turn off command output. This is done only
     because some batch files I use are redirected to "nul".
   . I tried to make everything as compatible to MS-DOS as possible.
     If a format you use isn't supported- let me know and I will
     accomodate your needs.
   . Automatic saving of current directory, working directories, and
     DOSKEY history.
   . The LABEL command is inactive because writing to the LABEL of
     a C: drive can trigger any bootsector virus checkers causing
     your system to hang.
   . Now allows support for giving users their own DOS directories,
     as well as configuring which commands are available to them!
